From c0f1eeedc79482f8b51cebee478340d23923359c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:03:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1238/3799] soh: rename func_80094E54 ->
 Gfx_BranchTexScrollNoSize

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: forwards to Gfx_BranchTexScroll with width and height 0, so only the tile's scroll origin is set.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_rcp.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_rcp.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_rcp.c b/soh/src/code/z_rcp.c
index 9cd3905da..b584ad5f2 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_rcp.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_rcp.c
@@ -1375,7 +1375,8 @@ Gfx* Gfx_BranchTexScroll(Gfx** gfxp, u32 x, u32 y, s32 width, s32 height) {
     return displayList;
 }
 
-Gfx* func_80094E54(Gfx** gfxp, u32 x, u32 y) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80094E54: forwards to Gfx_BranchTexScroll with width and height 0, so only the tile's scroll origin is set.
+Gfx* Gfx_BranchTexScrollNoSize(Gfx** gfxp, u32 x, u32 y) {
     return Gfx_BranchTexScroll(gfxp, x, y, 0, 0);
 }
 
